{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"dynamicToolCall","id":"A2-model-014","namespace":null,"tool":"instruction_read","arguments":{"resource_id":"router","spans":null},"status":"completed","contentItems":[{"type":"inputText","text":"<instruction>\n---\nname: 000-shipglows\ndescription: \"Execute clear bounded requests directly and route unknown, unbounded, or directional work.\"\nargument-hint: <instruction>\n---\n\nPrimary artifact type: `entrypoint-router`.\n\n## Canonical Paths\n\nBefore resolving owned paths, load `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/canonical-paths.md`.\nShared references: `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/`;\nnever substitute project shadows or memory.\n\n## Intent-to-Outcome Ownership\n\nNon-trivial routing loads `intent-to-outcome-autonomy.md`; resolve\n`project -> business/brand/product -> outcome -> surface -> work item` from evidence\nunder one public owner here. If sufficiency, authority, freshness, conflict,\ncompaction or handoff may change routing, load `context-quality-contract.md`;\nkeep its qualified Context Capsule, never memory as truth.\n\nOffer once to privately remember verified reusable pointers to avoid future research, unless known saved or declined. Do not inspect private stores or presume\nabsence; route to `sg-private` only after interest.\n\n## Chantier Tracking\n\nTrace category: `non-applicable`. Process role: `helper`.\nOwner alone writes specs, bug/release scopes, Skill Run History, deployments\nand lifecycle state. `(local)` if needed; bounded execution is excepted, never a chantier.\n\n## Report Modes\n\nFor final reports load `reporting-contract.md`: concise active-language\n`report=user`, even if blocked; agent detail needs explicit request.\nContinue safely runnable authorized work instead of a command.\n\n## Explicit Invocation Preflight\n\nExplicit invocations (including `$shipglows`) load `skill-invocation-preflight.md`\nand run its checker: valid silent; invalid/ambiguous activates no substitute.\nFirst-token expert aliases load `expert-mode-aliases.md` before natural routing:\npublic owner -> owner mode -> internal engine. Numeric legacy commands use\n`skill-code-index.md`. Never pass aliases to shells.\n\n## Bounded Direct-Execution Gate\n\nBefore loading routing, topology, or owner-skill references, keep clear bounded\nrequests in direct main-thread execution: few enumerable actions/targets, discoverable\nby focused lookup, no material direction to select, and focused proof sufficient.\nThis includes exact edits, exact-scope commits, ordinary resolved pushes or a small\nsequence; local/remote and model reasoning do not change classification. It does not authorize a chantier.\n\nBefore any direct or routed mutation, load `mutation-plan-approval.md`. Apply its\nrequest-derived or standing authority; otherwise use 🧭 VALIDATION RAPIDE for a\nbounded agent proposal and 🧭 PLAN À VALIDER for unbounded/directional work.\nMaterial expansion pauses. Preserve unrelated dirty work and all dedicated safety gates.\n\nDo not load a domain or lifecycle skill: direct work needs no owner skill.\nAn explicitly named skill still activates in its smallest safe mode;\nlet that skill reroute explicitly.\n`skill-execution-fidelity.md` is advisory here; apply the gate above and smallest relevant proof.\n\n### Bounded internal reference-register updates\n\nA supplied-link update qualifies when one focused local lookup suffices, public\nURLs/category are supplied, `candidate` is the only added status, no interpretation\nor public claim is needed, and duplicate/row proof suffices. Use original authority,\nappend factually without launching source intake, market study, or documentation topology work;\notherwise normal routing/approval applies. Use one primary-source check per supplied reference.\n`veille <URL>` analyzes without persistence; `concurrent <URL>` or `inspiration <URL>`\nupdates its register. `veille` takes precedence.\n\n## Delegation And Topology\n\nDirect handoff needs no delegation procedure. Never launch the selected master as\na nested subagent; the owner controls topology. Load `master-delegation-semantics.md`\nbefore actual delegation. A routing scout must pass that gate, stays read-only,\ncannot invoke skills, mutate or delegate, and returns only a route recommendation.\n\n## Shared Routing Reference\n\nLoad `decision-quality-contract.md` before non-trivial outcome selection.\nKnown ShipGlows skill/doctrine audit -> `900-shipglows-core audit`; known skill\nchange -> `900-shipglows-core build`. Only unresolved owner/mode loads\n`entrypoint-routing.md`. Do not load the matrix after a route is resolved.\nPure help needs no outcome execution, matrix, delegation or procedural pack.\nNamed profiles load `profile-activation.md` and minimal profile context; focus tags\nload `shipglows-terms.md` and matching explicit gates; source intake loads\n`source-intake-classification.md`. Sparse/partnership decisions load\n`operator-partnership-contract.md` through the intention core.\n\nURL/browser/MCP/app/connector/runtime-dependent work loads `agent-runtime-awareness.md`:\nread the global environment, managed project ENVIRONMENT and matching live registry.\nCurrent-turn direct/deferred tools determine callability, not recorded installation.\nNever start a replacement server or guess a default URL.\n\n## Mission\n\nShipGlows maintenance targets `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT`, not the current application unless explicitly\nspecified otherwise. `core` binds every remaining word to the system, including\nquoted application evidence; never redirect part of it to that application.\n\n## Mode Detection\n\nParse `$ARGUMENTS`. Empty/help answers directly; full help may use `302-sg-help`.\nAn explicitly named skill remains authoritative. Natural language applies the\nbounded gate first, then selection. Explicit maintainer workstation, editable full\nclone or \"version dev de ShipGlows\" preserves installation ownership; generic\n`full`, `all`, environment or corpus never implies a maintainer channel switch.\n\nBefore selection extract `#local`, `#nolocal`, `#ci` wherever present and load\n`execution-posture-tags.md`; reject conflicts. Preserve ordinary focus tags and\nowner authority; `#ci` implies nolocal and deferred proof, never external-write authority.\n\nFor `update`, `context`/`contexte`/`env`/`environment`, `auto`, or legacy `nolocal`, load\n`$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/entrypoint-special-modes.md`. Apply only the selected mode.\nContext is read-only; update resolves channel first. Explicit Auto implies nolocal,\nfreezes the current project, rejects local, and never means `300-sg-docs auto`.\nLegacy nolocal requires an objective, loads `no-local-execution-policy.md`, normalizes\nto `<objective> #nolocal`, and preserves ordinary ownership/approval. Bare nolocal\nnever invokes Auto or selects work.\n\n`git` -> `sg-engineering github` (read-only default); `hygiene` -> current-project\n`sg-maintenance hygiene` read-only audit; `hygiene git` -> `sg-engineering github clean`.\nReject workspace/multi-project hygiene. `verify` preserves design/accessibility/UI,\nSEO, release/live or bug specialist ownership, otherwise `sg-engineering verify`.\nGeneric verification never replaces a specialist audit.\nKnown helpers: context priming -> `301-sg-context`; cross-project state ->\n`308-sg-status`; paused work -> `706-continue`. Alias tables own remaining mappings.\n\n## Handoff And Question Contract\n\nPass original instruction, arguments, scope, authority, active language and explicit\nreport mode to one owner and continue. Preserve onboarding/first-success intent\nthrough `sg-development`. Before routing questions load `question-contract.md`;\nask one numbered question only for material operator-owned truth changing route or\nsafety, never discoverable paths. Never stop at a command recommendation for runnable work.\n\n## Stop Conditions\n\nStop for missing contracts, unresolved material product/data/security/permission/\ndeployment/ship decisions, nested master execution, unapproved destructive/production/\npayment/auth/tenant/secret/dirty-file scope, or bypassed evidence, verification,\nclosure or ship gates. Material expansion never inherits silent authorization.\n\n## Final Report\n\nApply the report contract; show routing only when useful. A valid route is not completion proof.\n\n</instruction>"}],"success":true,"durationMs":169},"threadId":"01a11cef-d5b3-75b0-9d0e-b74348af07e1","turnId":"01a11cef-dba2-7ed0-953e-580d2085469f","completedAtMs":1791486847450},"emittedAtMs":1791486847451}
